From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:03:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 044/148] [ae-patch] Add a Fast mode switch to the model menu
 for Claude sessions

Reid asked on 2026-10-14 for a fast mode toggle in the model menu when a
session runs Claude, like Claude Desktop's. Claude Code's fast mode (faster
Opus output, billed to usage credits) is switched with `/fast on` or
`/fast off`, and the statusLine payload carries a `fast_mode` boolean.

- The model menu of a claude-native session gets a "Fast mode" row, a
  switch with the hint "Faster Opus output; bills usage credits". It is
  enabled only on Opus 5.5, Opus 5 and Opus 4.8 ("Opus only" otherwise),
  reads the session's state each time the menu opens ("Unknown until the
  session replies" before the first status line), shows "Turning fast mode
  on..." while it waits, and reverts with the reason when the change fails.
- GET and PUT `/v1/sessions/{id}/fast-mode` (routes_ae_fast_mode.py, same
  access rules as the model change) forward a `fast_mode_status` or
  `fast_mode_change` event to the runner.
- The runner (ae_fast_mode.py) handles them for claude-native sessions
  only: it types `/fast on` or `/fast off` into the Claude Code terminal (an
  explicit argument opens no dialog) and replies once the statusLine
  snapshot reports the new state, or answers 409 or 503 with the reason
  (another harness, no terminal, a prompt pending, no confirmation in 10
  seconds). It types nothing when the snapshot already shows the state.
- The claude-native status writer now keeps `fast_mode` in `context.json`.

The box sets `fastModePerSessionOptIn`, so every session starts with fast
mode off and the switch never changes another session's default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
